      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="what-trainerize-lists-today">
        <h2>What Trainerize lists today</h2>
        <p>Trainerize has been part of ABC Fitness since September 2020, according to its <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/about/" rel="noopener">About page</a>. It lists a free plan for 1 client, a 30-day free trial with unlimited clients, and paid plans priced by number of clients, from Grow (2 clients) through Pro to Studio Plus, with a 10% discount for annual billing.</p>
        <p>Its AI Workout Builder is included from the Grow plan up. FitMetrics, which Trainerize calls <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/blog/ai-coaching-software-with-coach-control/" rel="noopener">"a new AI add-on"</a>, drafts check-in replies. Trainerize's <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/features/fitmetrics/" rel="noopener">FitMetrics page</a> says "By default, you review every drafted reply before anything sends to a client." The same page says: "Link your website or upload your own Q&amp;A knowledge base, and the AI Assistant learns your approach and tone so its drafts sound like you."</p>
        <p>FitMetrics is a paid add-on. Trainerize's public pages currently describe FitMetrics pricing differently, so this page does not state a FitMetrics price. Check <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/features/fitmetrics/" rel="noopener">Trainerize</a> for current pricing.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="what-to-compare">
        <h2>What to compare</h2>
        <ul class="c-dots">
          <li><b>Client limits.</b> How many clients each plan allows, at your client count now and the count you expect.</li>
          <li><b>Add-ons.</b> Which features are included and which are billed separately.</li>
          <li><b>AI.</b> What it does, whether you review its output before a client sees it, and how usage is billed.</li>
          <li><b>Branding.</b> Whether you get custom branding inside the provider's app or your own app-store listing, which plan includes it, and any fee.</li>
          <li><b>Payments.</b> Built in or an add-on, and the provider's current processing fees.</li>
          <li><b>Integrations.</b> The wearables, nutrition apps and automation tools you already use.</li>
          <li><b>Exercise library.</b> Whether demos are included, and whether you can add your own.</li>
          <li><b>Trial or free plan.</b> Length, client limit, whether a card is required, and which features the trial includes.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="alternatives-to-trainerize-in-alphabetical-order">
        <h2>Alternatives to Trainerize, in alphabetical order</h2>
        <section class="c-provider" id="everfit">
          <h3>Everfit</h3>
          <p>Everfit lists a free Starter plan for up to 5 clients. Pro runs from $19 per month for 5 clients to $290 per month for 300 clients on monthly billing, and Studio runs from $105 per month for 50 clients to $430 per month for 500 clients. Its exercise library lists 1,000+ exercises, and coaches can create their own.</p>
          <p>Everfit's <a href="https://everfit.io/integration/" rel="noopener">integrations page</a> names Apple Health, Google Health, Apple Watch, Garmin, Fitbit, WHOOP, Oura, MyFitnessPal, Cronometer, Stripe and Zapier. Its help center says Zapier is available <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/8543585-introducing-zapier-integration" rel="noopener">"as a Plugin on the Studio plan"</a> and that <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/15176278-everfit-api-integration-guide" rel="noopener">API access</a> is for Enterprise customers. Payments are an add-on, and Everfit's <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/5684968-processing-fees-for-payments" rel="noopener">payment fees page</a> lists an Everfit platform fee of USD $9 per month. Everfit lists Custom Branding on Pro and Studio, and its <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/5754312-advanced-custom-branding-bring-your-brand-to-the-next-level" rel="noopener">help center</a> lists Advanced Custom Branding as a $75 one-time add-on for Pro and Studio and points coaches who want their own app listings to its white-label solution on Enterprise.</p>
          <p>Everfit lists an AI Workout Builder that turns notes or PDFs into a program, and Smart Response, which Everfit describes as <a href="https://everfit.io/ai-suite/" rel="noopener">"AI-drafted replies in your voice"</a> that coaches "just review, edit, and send." Its <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/13212021-ai-smart-response" rel="noopener">help center</a> says drafts can draw on the coach's Knowledge Base and Saved Responses. Smart Response is <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/16881431-ai-smart-response-credits-and-plans" rel="noopener">credit based and billed per coach</a>: each coach on an eligible paid plan gets 50 free credits per month, and a paid seat, assigned to a specific coach, includes 250, 1,200 or 3,500 credits per month for $15, $50 or $100 per month. Everfit says Smart Response is not available on Trial or Starter workspaces.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="c-provider" id="my-pt-hub">
          <h3>My PT Hub</h3>
          <p>My PT Hub lists a free Lite plan for 1 client, Starter for 3 clients at $25 per month on flexible monthly billing, and Premium and Ultimate with unlimited clients at $59 and $215 per month. On annual billing paid monthly, the three paid plans list at $22.50, $52 and $195 per month. Introductory promotions shown on the page, on plan prices and on the branded app fee, are not included here.</p>
          <p>Its <a href="https://www.mypthub.net/pricing/" rel="noopener">pricing page</a> lists an AI workout builder and Nutrition AI on Premium and Ultimate. Check-Ins AI, described as "AI-powered check-ins," is a $12 per month add-on on Premium and is listed on Ultimate with no separate price. The pricing page says it can "Generate responses to clients in seconds using AI," and My PT Hub's <a href="https://www.mypthub.net/all-updates/" rel="noopener">product updates page</a> says Check-Ins AI lets AI "draft personalized feedback that you can review, regenerate, or edit before sending." Payment processing through Stripe is listed on Starter, Premium and Ultimate. Zapier is a $19 per month add-on on Premium and is listed on Ultimate with no separate price, and the page lists wearable integrations. Its <a href="https://www.mypthub.net/features/workout-features/" rel="noopener">workout features page</a> lists "over 8,000 HD exercise videos" and says trainers can upload their own.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="c-provider" id="truecoach">
          <h3>TrueCoach</h3>
          <p>TrueCoach lists Starter, Standard and Pro plans for up to 5, 20 and 50 active clients, at $29.98, $69.98 and $164.98 per month billed monthly, or $26.34, $57.99 and $136.99 per month billed annually. It also lists a 14-day free trial and a 90-day money-back guarantee on annual plans for first-time subscribers, subject to its <a href="https://truecoach.co/truecoach-guarantee-terms/" rel="noopener">terms</a>.</p>
          <p>Its <a href="https://truecoach.co/pricing/" rel="noopener">pricing page</a> lists a video exercise library and says coaches can upload their own videos. Payments run through Stripe on all plans, and the branded app and wearable integrations (Apple, Garmin, WHOOP and others) are on Standard and Pro. Its <a href="https://truecoach.co/about/" rel="noopener">About page</a> says TrueCoach is "Powered by Xplor Technologies."</p>
        </section>
        <section class="c-provider" id="wolvec">
          <h3>Wolvec</h3>
          <p>Wolvec is an AI platform for fitness coaches and online personal trainers, the whole coaching setup rather than an add-on to it. Your AI is built from one conversation about how you coach, so you can start without a content library.</p>
          <p>Depending on the chat level you choose, your AI can answer routine questions based on how you coach, draft a reply for you to review, or stay off. The catalog comes with animated demos and step-by-step instructions, so you are not filming or writing them up yourself.</p>
          <p>Some of this overlaps with other platforms on this page. Trainerize, Everfit and My PT Hub list AI reply drafts that the coach reviews before sending, and Trainerize, Everfit, My PT Hub and TrueCoach list exercise libraries. The others also publish pricing and list free plans or trials, payments, branded apps and integrations, which this page does not cover for Wolvec. Wolvec does not currently publish pricing, and this page makes no statement about whether any Wolvec feature is included in a base price or carries a separate charge.</p>
          <p>Wolvec is in early access by invitation.</p>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="looking-for-an-everfit-alternative">
        <h2>Looking for an Everfit alternative?</h2>
        <p>Alternatives to Everfit on this page are My PT Hub, Trainerize, TrueCoach and Wolvec. Everfit lists a free plan for up to 5 clients and credit-based AI replies, so compare free plan client limits and how each provider bills for AI.</p>
        <p>For Everfit and Trainerize side by side, see <a href="/compare/everfit-vs-trainerize">Everfit vs Trainerize</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="looking-for-a-truecoach-alternative">
        <h2>Looking for a TrueCoach alternative?</h2>
        <p>The other platforms on this page are also alternatives to TrueCoach: Everfit, My PT Hub, Trainerize and Wolvec. Compare TrueCoach's active-client limits (5, 20 and 50) with how each one counts clients, and check which plan includes the branded app and integrations.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="frequently-asked-questions">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="c-faq">
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>Is there a free alternative to Trainerize?</h3>
          <p>Everfit lists a Starter plan that is free for up to 5 clients, and My PT Hub lists a free Lite plan for 1 client. Trainerize itself lists a free plan for 1 client. TrueCoach lists a 14-day free trial.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>Does Wolvec publish pricing?</h3>
          <p>Wolvec does not currently publish pricing. Wolvec is in early access by invitation.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </section>

